🔹 Spark Interview Q&A Revision Guide

1. Basics

1. What is Apache Spark, and how is it different from Hadoop MapReduce?
👉 Spark is a distributed computing framework, faster than MapReduce due to in-memory processing and DAG execution.

2. What are RDDs (Resilient Distributed Datasets)?
👉 Immutable, fault-tolerant, distributed collections of objects; core abstraction in Spark.

3. Advantages of Spark?
👉 Speed (in-memory),
 fault tolerance,
 support for SQL, ML, streaming, and graph processing,
 easy APIs (Java, Scala, Python, R),

4. Components of Spark?
👉 Spark Core, Spark SQL, Spark Streaming, MLlib (machine learning), GraphX (graph processing).

5. Difference between RDD, DataFrame, and Dataset?
👉 RDD = low-level, untyped, functional API.
👉 DataFrame = tabular, optimized, schema-aware.
👉 Dataset = strongly typed (Scala/Java), combines benefits of RDD + DataFrame.

JavaRDD<String> lines = sc.textFile("data.txt");
JavaRDD<Integer> lengths = lines.map(String::length);

Dataset<Row> df = spark.read().json("people.json");
df.select("name", "age").where("age > 25").show();

Dataset<Person> ds = spark.read().json("people.json").as(Encoders.bean(Person.class));
ds.filter(p -> p.getAge() > 25).show();

