2. RDD & Transformations

6. Transformations vs Actions?
👉 Transformations (lazy, return new RDD, e.g. map, filter), Actions (trigger execution, return result, e.g. collect, count).

7. Lazy evaluation?
👉 Spark builds a DAG of transformations and executes only when an action is called.

8. Narrow vs Wide transformations?
👉 Narrow = no shuffle (e.g. map, filter).
👉 Wide = needs shuffle across partitions (e.g. groupByKey, reduceByKey).

9. Data partitioning?
👉 Spark splits data into partitions distributed across cluster nodes.

10. Optimize partitions?
👉 Use repartition() (increase partitions), coalesce() (decrease partitions), and tune partition count based on data size & cluster resources.

