3. Spark Architecture

11. Spark architecture components?
👉 Driver (coordinates job), Executors (run tasks), Cluster Manager (YARN, Mesos, Kubernetes, Standalone).

12. Fault tolerance?
👉 Spark uses lineage info to recompute lost partitions + replication in memory.

13. Lineage in Spark?
👉 DAG of transformations that tells Spark how to recompute lost data.

14. Spark memory management?
👉 Divided into execution memory (caching, shuffles) and storage memory (RDD cache, broadcast).

15. DAG in Spark?
👉 Directed Acyclic Graph of stages and tasks Spark generates before execution.

⸻

4. Spark SQL & DataFrames

16. Spark SQL vs Hive?
👉 Spark SQL runs queries faster with Catalyst optimizer; Hive uses MapReduce (slower).

17. Creating DataFrame?
👉 From RDD (spark.createDataFrame(rdd)), from file (spark.read.json/parquet/csv), from table.

18. Catalyst Optimizer?
👉 Query optimizer in Spark SQL: does logical & physical plan optimization.

19. Tungsten?
👉 Project for memory & code generation optimizations (off-heap, whole-stage codegen).

20. cache() vs persist()?
👉 cache() = shorthand for persist(MEMORY_ONLY).
👉 persist() = allows custom storage levels.

