5. Performance & Optimization

21. Handle data skew?
👉 Use salting, repartitioning, broadcast joins, avoiding wide shuffles.

22. Techniques to optimize jobs?
👉 Use partitioning, caching, broadcast variables, reduce shuffles, predicate pushdown.

23. Predicate pushdown?
👉 Filter conditions are pushed to the data source level (e.g. Parquet, ORC) → less data read.

24. Broadcast join?
👉 Small dataset is broadcast to all executors → avoids shuffle for large joins.

25. Shuffle in Spark?
👉 Re-distribution of data across partitions during wide transformations; costly operation.

